WEBVTT

00:12.970 --> 00:18.710
Hikari ga sasu sora, umareochiru kage
In the bright sky illuminated by
sunlight, darkened shadows are born.

00:18.810 --> 00:24.150
Unmei wa dokomademo hikisakareru
Fate itself is being torn apart.

00:25.190 --> 00:30.150
Donna toki mo kesshite akiramenainara
If you never give up, no matter what happens,

00:30.330 --> 00:37.560
mada tozasareteru tobira kanarazu hiraku
Even that locked door will open for you.

00:38.530 --> 00:43.990
Eien datte dakishimete, fuuin mo tokihanachi
Embrace eternity and release the seal.

00:44.070 --> 00:49.940
Mamorubekimono ga ima kokoni wa arukara
Because the ones you wish
to protect are right here.

00:49.940 --> 00:55.880
Namida mo gyutto dakishimete,
yasashisa de tsutsumikomi
Embrace their tears with kindness.

00:55.880 --> 01:01.560
Nagareru mizu no youni tsuyoku nare
Become strong like the formless water,

01:01.560 --> 01:07.550
omouyouni tsuyoku nare
Become as strong as you wish to be.

01:07.700 --> 01:13.170
Mou jibun ni obienaide
Stop being afraid of yourself.

01:13.170 --> 01:19.800
Sou mirai wo osorenaide
Do not fear the future.

01:33.760 --> 01:34.860
Radio Exercise Program

01:34.860 --> 01:35.690
Radio Exercise Program
I think I might get perfect attendance this year.

01:35.690 --> 01:37.210
I think I might get perfect attendance this year.

01:42.860 --> 01:45.830
Feeling...

01:47.270 --> 01:50.360
Kinda...

01:50.540 --> 01:53.940
Sorta...

01:54.680 --> 01:57.440
Happy!

02:03.750 --> 02:07.210
Young man! Do you feel happy?!

02:07.460 --> 02:12.420
Our Fox Deity, Goes on a Search

02:17.900 --> 02:20.700
She might not be human...

02:22.340 --> 02:24.310
I'm asking if you're happy or not!

02:25.710 --> 02:29.940
Well, I can't make such a sweeping generalization...

02:29.940 --> 02:32.040
...but if I had to choose,
I would say that I'm not miserable.

02:32.380 --> 02:33.750
Oh, really?

02:33.750 --> 02:37.980
If you can say for sure you're not miserable,
then you're happy.

02:38.390 --> 02:41.010
As for me, I'm really miserable right now!

02:42.160 --> 02:43.060
Why?

02:43.060 --> 02:47.390
I'm sad because my Sakasaen went missing!

02:48.000 --> 02:52.060
Sakasaen... Where did I hear that before?

02:52.130 --> 02:56.700
Hey, young man. Won't you help me find it?!

02:57.610 --> 03:01.270
Maybe she's not a bad person, I guess...

03:02.610 --> 03:03.940
Sure.

03:04.250 --> 03:06.910
Really?! Thanks!

03:07.280 --> 03:09.180
But what does it look like?

03:09.180 --> 03:11.410
It's round! Because it's a ring!

03:13.020 --> 03:15.320
And how are you going to find it?

03:19.530 --> 03:23.230
You have a smart fox at your home, right?

03:23.230 --> 03:25.260
Let's ask it for help.

03:26.070 --> 03:27.560
Who are you?

03:27.900 --> 03:32.460
I'm Mubyo. I'm the god of the land next door.

03:33.210 --> 03:37.610
The Sakasaen is an item that
reverses the Five Phases.

03:38.180 --> 03:40.650
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:40.650 --> 03:41.220
Wood
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:41.220 --> 03:41.650
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:41.650 --> 03:42.250
Fire
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:42.250 --> 03:42.620
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:42.620 --> 03:43.220
Earth
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:43.220 --> 03:43.620
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:43.620 --> 03:44.250
Metal
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:44.250 --> 03:44.620
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:44.620 --> 03:45.290
Water
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:45.290 --> 03:48.020
The five elements go in the order of
wood, fire, earth, metal, and water.

03:48.020 --> 03:51.250
The Sakasaen lets you go in the opposite direction.

03:53.630 --> 03:55.260
I don't really get it.

03:55.600 --> 03:58.190
And that thing was stolen from me.

03:58.470 --> 04:05.370
It's unlikely for anyone to be able abuse it,
but it can be dangerous in the wrong hands.

04:06.610 --> 04:13.040
Besides, it's something really precious to me,
so I have to find it.

04:13.180 --> 04:14.210
Oh.

04:15.850 --> 04:17.650
Now I remember, Mubyo-san.

04:18.090 --> 04:23.110
No need to be so polite! Just call me Mubyo-chan!

04:23.460 --> 04:28.990
Okay, Mubyo-chan. Weren't you the one who
put out a headhunt for a clam yokai last month?

04:29.630 --> 04:34.500
I thought that clam guy was the
one who stole the Sakasaen.

04:35.070 --> 04:41.530
A friend of mine then caught it and
brought the clam to you, didn't he?

04:42.380 --> 04:43.140
He did.

04:43.540 --> 04:44.250
Then...

04:44.250 --> 04:48.450
But that clam didn't know where the Sakasaen was!

04:48.450 --> 04:52.580
He had some raccoon dog co-conspirator hide it!

04:52.790 --> 04:55.480
But then he disappeared off to somewhere.

04:58.490 --> 04:59.430
I'm home!

04:59.890 --> 05:02.620
Toru!

05:03.000 --> 05:04.620
Welcome home!

05:05.870 --> 05:06.660
Ku-chan...

05:08.200 --> 05:09.690
What happened to you?

05:10.740 --> 05:16.770
I want to go to this placed called the "pool!"

05:17.710 --> 05:20.340
Let's go! Come on, let's go! Please?

05:24.690 --> 05:26.650
Who are you?

05:35.960 --> 05:37.490
Sounds like a pain in the ass, so no.

05:38.100 --> 05:39.370
What?!

05:39.370 --> 05:42.800
Why do I have to help you?

05:42.800 --> 05:47.680
You're partially responsible for
making the Sakasaen so hard to find!

05:47.680 --> 05:48.380
What?

05:48.380 --> 05:51.000
You performed the Spirit Passing spell, didn't you?

05:52.080 --> 05:54.780
The effects of that spell came to my land...

05:54.780 --> 05:56.680
...and completely screwed up the
flow of the air and spiritual energy.

05:56.680 --> 06:00.640
You made it really hard for
the gods to use their powers.

06:01.190 --> 06:03.830
It's just really hard to find anything right now!

06:03.830 --> 06:06.560
That's a bit of a stretch. How is it my fault?

06:06.690 --> 06:08.790
Don't try to weasel out of this!

06:09.200 --> 06:13.670
Besides, I hate you gods.

06:13.670 --> 06:15.840
What? Now you're picking a fight with me?

06:15.840 --> 06:17.770
W-Wait!

06:18.410 --> 06:20.970
Ku-chan, let's help her.

06:22.680 --> 06:26.340
You're so nice, Toru-chan!

06:26.550 --> 06:28.140
Toru?

06:28.220 --> 06:32.150
W-Well, because...

06:32.150 --> 06:37.820
I heard the Sakasaen can be really dangerous.
And Mubyo-chan really needs help...

06:37.930 --> 06:39.520
So that's why...

06:54.640 --> 06:56.630
A raccoon dog?

06:58.750 --> 07:01.510
That guy might not be human...

07:06.050 --> 07:09.190
You are the head of the Mizuchi family, I presume.

07:09.190 --> 07:10.180
No, I'm not.

07:13.160 --> 07:16.820
Hold on! You're the head of
the Mizuchi family, right?

07:17.770 --> 07:19.630
No. Seriously, you got the wrong person.

07:20.070 --> 07:23.060
Why are you lying to me? Wait!

07:23.300 --> 07:25.270
I'm not done talking...

07:26.210 --> 07:26.970
Hey!

07:27.580 --> 07:28.410
Hey!

07:31.650 --> 07:34.980
Wh-Why is he running from me?

07:35.480 --> 07:39.680
The Sakasaen? You still haven't found it yet?

07:39.920 --> 07:43.950
That's why we were wondering
if you knew anything about it.

07:44.460 --> 07:47.120
What are you doing here, anyway?

07:47.700 --> 07:51.030
I thought you were ordered to stay in Akagi.

07:51.570 --> 07:52.060
Ordered?

07:54.540 --> 07:59.560
Stop it right there or I'll crush that rotten
head of yours with my bare hands!

08:01.010 --> 08:02.100
Just kidding!

08:03.110 --> 08:08.910
Unfortunately, I don't know anything
and I can't help you either way.

08:10.080 --> 08:12.450
I'm busy trying to maintain my own land.

08:12.790 --> 08:16.090
The aftereffects of the Spirit
Passing are still lingering.

08:16.660 --> 08:19.790
If you got a problem with me,
why don't you say it to my face?

08:19.890 --> 08:21.620
Problem? What problem?

08:21.860 --> 08:24.390
That's that. Sorry, Toru-kun.

08:25.530 --> 08:30.810
Geez! That's why I said going
to Ebi-chan is a waste of time!

08:30.810 --> 08:34.240
Hey, Toru. Why don't we go to the pool instead?

08:34.710 --> 08:36.300
You want to come too, right?

08:36.480 --> 08:37.740
I don't!

08:38.210 --> 08:40.580
What? You don't like pools?

08:42.080 --> 08:43.520
I get it!

08:47.760 --> 08:50.990
You don't have any feminine parts!

08:52.360 --> 08:55.330
That's why you're wearing thick clothing!

08:55.330 --> 08:58.390
And because of that,
you hate going to the pool, too.

09:00.270 --> 09:02.930
I completely understand now!

09:03.070 --> 09:07.940
No! You want to die, you stupid fox?!

09:07.940 --> 09:10.310
Hey, Ku! Toru!

09:10.750 --> 09:12.370
Oh, hey.

09:12.610 --> 09:15.210
What are you panicking about?

09:15.420 --> 09:20.480
I saw some weird guy near the school!
He's definitely a yokai!

09:20.620 --> 09:24.490
He was dressed all in black and
wore this raccoon dog mask...

09:25.360 --> 09:26.290
That's him!

09:26.530 --> 09:27.520
Mubyo-chan?

09:27.930 --> 09:30.960
You remember how I said the
clam's partner was a raccoon dog?

09:31.270 --> 09:33.670
That uniform means you're from Akagi High, right?!

09:33.670 --> 09:36.370
You saw that raccoon dog near the school?!

09:36.370 --> 09:37.960
Awesome!

09:38.340 --> 09:40.810
Anyway, let's go! To Akagi!

09:40.810 --> 09:43.570
No. We're going home, Toru.

09:45.480 --> 09:49.070
Akagi is your territory.
You can go find it on your own.

09:49.380 --> 09:52.680
No! I can't! It's impossible!

09:52.820 --> 09:53.480
Why?

09:53.790 --> 09:56.490
Because of... Uhh...

09:56.490 --> 09:59.520
Oh yeah! I know!

09:59.730 --> 10:03.320
Did you forget that the effects of
the Spirit Passing are still lingering?

10:03.560 --> 10:05.190
It's all your fault!

10:05.370 --> 10:07.030
Look...

10:07.400 --> 10:09.160
Let's help her.

10:09.500 --> 10:15.240
Toru, why are you going out
of your way to help her?

10:17.750 --> 10:21.240
Ku-chan performed the Spirit Passing for me.

10:23.520 --> 10:27.540
That's why the store owner and
Mubyo-chan are both in trouble.

10:29.420 --> 10:32.790
If Ku-chan doesn't want to do it, I can't force her.

10:33.590 --> 10:37.430
But I won't be able to help her much on my own...

10:39.570 --> 10:43.560
Fine. If you insist.

10:44.570 --> 10:47.130
Thank you, Toru-chan!

10:59.020 --> 11:03.080
Akagi High School

11:03.620 --> 11:05.220
You can't go in, okay?

11:05.390 --> 11:09.920
I know. If you tell me not to, I won't.

11:10.870 --> 11:12.090
Noboru-san!

11:12.530 --> 11:13.660
Ogami-san?

11:13.970 --> 11:17.460
Toru-san and Tenko-sama. Mubyo-sama, too?!

11:17.840 --> 11:19.930
What are you all doing here?

11:20.170 --> 11:23.040
I should be asking you the same thing.

11:23.240 --> 11:28.420
Mubyo-sama arranged for me to work
and live here starting last month!

11:28.420 --> 11:30.950
Oh, really? I didn't notice at all.

11:30.950 --> 11:32.750
How is Daigoro-chan doing?

11:32.890 --> 11:38.050
Very well! Mubyo-sama even
provided lots of toys for him!

11:38.530 --> 11:41.500
Daigoro is in the night-shift room right now.

11:41.500 --> 11:44.070
Sorry. We're a bit busy right now...

11:44.070 --> 11:48.470
I see. Well, please come visit anytime!

11:48.470 --> 11:51.200
I have to return to work, so good-bye!

11:51.740 --> 11:53.100
Bye-bye!

11:54.580 --> 11:57.440
Where do you want to start looking?

12:01.950 --> 12:04.950
Noboru! That! That!

12:04.950 --> 12:05.820
What?

12:06.120 --> 12:08.180
Is that the pool?!

12:08.590 --> 12:09.450
Yeah, why?

12:09.960 --> 12:12.290
Schools have pools, too?!

12:12.760 --> 12:16.700
Come on, Noboru. I want to swim in the pool.

12:16.700 --> 12:20.060
What do I have to do to get in? Tell me.

12:20.330 --> 12:22.460
You're really pushing it, you know that?

12:24.970 --> 12:27.460
Where did those two go?

12:27.580 --> 12:28.670
Oh, no!

12:33.910 --> 12:35.180
Where am I?

12:35.750 --> 12:38.580
Don't get mad at me, Toru-chan.

12:40.390 --> 12:44.130
I actually know where the Sakasaen is.

12:44.130 --> 12:45.750
What? Really?

12:45.890 --> 12:49.330
The clam told me everything...

12:49.700 --> 12:52.760
I've known where it is since last month.

12:53.030 --> 12:54.330
Oh, really.

12:54.740 --> 12:56.440
So where is it?

12:56.440 --> 12:59.930
Inside your head.

13:00.880 --> 13:02.140
Oh...

13:02.680 --> 13:05.670
Noboru! Say it's all right for me to enter the school!

13:06.780 --> 13:09.550
I said you're my master, didn't I?!

13:09.550 --> 13:13.880
As long as you forbade me
to enter the school, I can't!

13:14.090 --> 13:17.580
So, say it! Say I can enter the school!

13:17.890 --> 13:20.090
You're telling me to order you to do something?

13:20.090 --> 13:21.320
Isn't that kind of backwards?

13:21.700 --> 13:24.360
Just do it! Toru's in danger!

13:25.400 --> 13:26.560
Fine!

13:26.900 --> 13:30.800
I don't know what's going on,
but you can go in the school!

13:34.280 --> 13:36.270
Hey! Wait for me, Ku!

13:36.610 --> 13:40.820
Just like how Ebi-chan said,
I can't enter Suzunose...

13:40.820 --> 13:44.580
...or intervene with any of the people of Suzunose.

13:45.950 --> 13:51.290
That's why I was waiting for you to come to Akagi.

13:51.290 --> 13:53.230
It felt like you'd never come.

13:54.530 --> 13:57.330
Are you sure it's in my head?

13:57.830 --> 13:59.320
That's what I heard.

13:59.870 --> 14:00.860
Then...

14:01.370 --> 14:05.270
Yup. I'm going to have to dig through your head.

14:05.570 --> 14:08.840
But if you do that, won't I...

14:08.840 --> 14:10.040
Don't worry.

14:10.310 --> 14:13.310
I really like you.

14:13.310 --> 14:22.920
So I'll ask for you to be reborn into
a happier and wealthier family.

14:26.090 --> 14:26.920
Ogami-san?

14:38.970 --> 14:40.770
Thanks, Ogami-san.

14:40.880 --> 14:46.640
But I wonder why Mubyo-chan thinks
the Sakasaen is inside my head.

14:47.080 --> 14:48.710
Is it even true?

14:49.020 --> 14:51.420
Wait, it's not?!

14:51.790 --> 14:55.220
Hmm. I don't think it is...

14:55.660 --> 14:58.560
But if Mubyo-chan says so...

14:58.560 --> 15:00.690
Dammit, which is it?

15:01.960 --> 15:06.160
I hid it in the night-shift room at
this school about a month ago.

15:06.600 --> 15:09.540
And it just disappeared...

15:10.000 --> 15:13.060
Who would put it inside your head anyway?

15:13.310 --> 15:18.340
Uh, Ogami-san?

15:20.550 --> 15:24.140
Ku! Where did you go?

15:27.050 --> 15:28.650
O-Ogami-san?!

15:38.730 --> 15:39.990
Daigoro-chan?

15:40.970 --> 15:43.770
Are you telling me he's not really Ogami-san?!

15:47.010 --> 15:49.130
You little brat...

15:51.950 --> 15:53.440
The Sakasaen!

15:56.520 --> 15:58.110
Give it back!

15:59.850 --> 16:01.080
Wait!

16:01.360 --> 16:05.520
D-Daigoro-chan... You got so much heavier.

16:07.630 --> 16:10.120
Wait!

16:37.320 --> 16:39.490
A raccoon dog?

16:41.460 --> 16:42.190
Are you okay?

16:42.500 --> 16:44.830
Yeah. Thanks, Ku-chan.

16:45.070 --> 16:50.000
Tenko Kugen! Takagami Toru! Freeze!

16:54.310 --> 17:00.080
Hooray! It worked! I knew I
can do it if I put my mind to it!

17:00.810 --> 17:03.980
It's not even your true name,
but you let the kotodama capture you.

17:03.980 --> 17:06.510
You've certainly waned, oh-great-Tenko-sama.

17:06.890 --> 17:11.880
Well, this is the land of Mubyo!
We're at an advantage here!

17:12.130 --> 17:13.890
Stop with that stupid act.

17:14.730 --> 17:17.820
What's the meaning of this?
Why are you after Toru?

17:18.170 --> 17:21.290
Toru-chan has the Sakasaen inside his head.

17:22.670 --> 17:26.160
Mubyo-chan! That's not true! The Sakasaen is...

17:26.510 --> 17:31.100
Toru-chan. You remember that dream
with that clam about a month ago?

17:31.610 --> 17:36.740
He said he left the Sakasaen
inside your head at that time.

17:37.750 --> 17:42.380
So you came all the way to the
neighboring land to lure Toru into Akagi?

17:42.860 --> 17:45.550
Ding-ding! Correct!

17:45.990 --> 17:48.290
The Sakasaen is right here!

17:49.200 --> 17:50.690
Keep your mouth shut, Toru.

17:51.130 --> 17:55.200
I thought you couldn't enter the school.

17:55.200 --> 17:57.100
Did you go against your master's orders?

17:57.500 --> 18:01.630
I'm not disobeying him. I made him say I can go in.

18:03.110 --> 18:04.200
What?

18:04.710 --> 18:08.170
Either way, I'm going to take back the Sakasaen.

18:08.750 --> 18:11.240
Listen to me, Mubyo-chan!

18:12.220 --> 18:15.120
Don't underestimate me.

18:19.590 --> 18:22.460
There's two Ku-chans?! What's going on?!

18:22.730 --> 18:26.600
This is just a mirage.

18:26.830 --> 18:29.800
I'm the mirage and that one is real.

18:30.100 --> 18:34.540
I'm not stupid enough to go
inside your territory unprepared.

18:45.050 --> 18:47.180
Hey! I can move now.

18:51.530 --> 18:53.960
This is the end of you!

19:04.510 --> 19:07.130
You were too fixated on the decoy.

19:07.540 --> 19:10.610
You completely lost your focus on us.

19:10.610 --> 19:12.980
And now your spell has been lifted.

19:13.980 --> 19:16.110
You were the real one all along.

19:16.420 --> 19:20.980
That's right. The fake is real and the real is fake...

19:21.320 --> 19:24.020
Quite a well-made mirage, don't you think?

19:24.260 --> 19:27.850
I've been getting this ready
ever since I set foot in Akagi.

19:29.400 --> 19:31.490
That clam has a grudge on us.

19:32.330 --> 19:36.330
He's just using you to get his revenge.

19:36.670 --> 19:41.700
Besides, do you really think a human would
be alive with the Sakasaen in his head?

19:42.210 --> 19:46.870
You're a presiding deity,
and you fell for such a stupid lie.

19:47.310 --> 19:49.580
What are you going to do with me?

19:51.520 --> 19:55.180
You should know that deicide is a serious crime.

19:55.360 --> 19:57.160
One that doesn't even
compare to the Spirit Passing.

19:57.160 --> 20:00.020
All gods in existence will come for your head.

20:01.860 --> 20:05.490
Between my anger at you for trying to kill Toru...

20:06.530 --> 20:10.700
...and the desire to avoid conflicts with the gods.

20:11.040 --> 20:16.500
It's just a matter of putting those two on
a scale and seeing which one is heavier.

20:17.380 --> 20:21.070
Don't bother asking which one I picked.
You should already know the answer.

20:25.050 --> 20:26.020
You're a fool.

20:29.120 --> 20:29.950
Wait!

20:35.700 --> 20:36.560
Here.

20:38.970 --> 20:40.760
The Sakasaen!

20:41.130 --> 20:42.000
Toru?!

20:44.740 --> 20:46.070
Y-You sure?

20:50.180 --> 20:52.910
Thank goodness...

20:53.450 --> 20:55.710
Now he'll compliment me again...

20:56.020 --> 20:58.680
Thank you. Thank you...

20:59.290 --> 21:00.410
I'm happy for you.

21:01.560 --> 21:05.920
You're always so...

21:08.330 --> 21:09.900
The roof...

21:09.900 --> 21:12.800
The roof is a complete mess!

21:12.800 --> 21:15.460
Toru! Ku! Are you okay?!

21:17.070 --> 21:17.970
Noboru!

21:17.970 --> 21:20.700
Noboru-san! It's that raccoon dog!

21:21.110 --> 21:23.800
That raccoon dog disguised himself as me and!

21:36.360 --> 21:42.820
Sora no hate ga tsunagaru basho wo
Where the horizon meets the earth,

21:43.300 --> 21:50.500
no ni saku hana wa mada kitto shiranai
The flower growing in the wild remains unaware.

21:51.870 --> 21:58.370
Kokoyori ii sekai ga aruto
While thinking that there
is a world better than this.

21:58.510 --> 22:06.150
Kokoro wa itsumo hane wo hirogetagaru
They always desire to spread
the wings of their hearts.

22:07.050 --> 22:14.050
Yume dakede owarasenai
Don't let it end as just a dream,

22:14.660 --> 22:21.160
chansu ga aru hazusa
There's always a chance.

22:21.400 --> 22:28.810
Daijoubu bokura wa hitori janai
It's all right. We are not alone.

22:28.810 --> 22:36.450
Kaze ga nanika wo iouto shiteru
The winds are telling us something.

22:36.450 --> 22:44.120
Daijoubu kanarazu umaku yareru
It's all right. You can do it.

22:44.120 --> 22:55.330
Omoi wa itsuka jibun wo kaeru michi ni naru
Those dreams are a path you'll change yourself.

23:06.310 --> 23:09.910
